{"name":"Instant Classic","hex":"#e3dac6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"instant","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very short period of time; a moment.","A single, usually precise, point in time."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Impending; imminent.","Urgent; pressing; acute."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instant"},{"term":"classic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to the first class or rank, especially in literature or art.","Exemplary of a particular style; defining a class or category; typical; archetypical; epitomic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perfect and/or early example of a particular style.","An artistic work of lasting worth, such as a film or song; a work of enduring excellence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/classic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Instant Classic","blocks":[{"text":"Instant Classic is an American barbershop quartet from Indianapolis, Indiana, comprising David Zimmerman, Theo Hicks, Kohl Kitzmiller and Kyle Kitzmiller."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant_Classic","wikidata":"Q28200523"},{"title":"Instant","blocks":[{"text":"In physics and the philosophy of science, instant refers to an infinitesimal interval in time, whose passage is instantaneous. In ordinary speech, an instant has been defined as \"a point or very short space of time,\" a notion deriving from its etymological source, the Latin verb instare, from in- + stare, meaning 'to stand upon or near.'"}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instant","wikidata":"Q16963779"},{"title":"Classic","blocks":[{"text":"A classic is an outstanding example of a particular style; something of lasting worth or with a timeless quality; of the first or highest quality, class, or rank – something that exemplifies its class. The word can be an adjective or a noun. It denotes a particular quality in art, architecture, literature, design, technology, or other cultural artifacts. In commerce, products are named 'classic' to denote a long-standing popular version or model, to distinguish it from a newer variety. Classic is used to describe many major, long-standing sporting events. Colloquially, an everyday occurrence may be described in some dialects of English as 'an absolute classic'."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classic","wikidata":"Q2976603"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"instant":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/20/En-us-instant.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/20/En-us-instant.ogg/En-us-instant.ogg.mp3"}],"classic":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-classic.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-classic.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-classic.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b2/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-classic.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-classic.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.404375},{"title":"Acanthite-40496","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/89/Acanthite-40496.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":0.8034782608695652,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Acanthite-40496.jpg","share":0.255625},{"title":"Classic cameras P1010936-KC100 (9151111019)","image":"https://thumb.wikim